{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Volatility: The model consistently forecasts a smooth, monotonic trend while true outcomes exhibit high-amplitude oscillations (spikes to 100+ and drops to 87+). Correction: Apply a volatility multiplier to the forecast range to capture the true swing magnitude.",
    "Lag in Mean Reversion: The model fails to anticipate sharp reversals immediately following price spikes (e.g., the drop from 100.12 to 96.30). Correction: Introduce a negative feedback term triggered when the 5-day rolling high exceeds the 20-day average by more than 5%.",
    "Sentiment Ignorance: Positive sentiment spikes (0.20-0.33) in the history do not correlate with the model's upward bias; the model remains static despite bullish signals. Correction: Weight the forecast slope positively when sentiment history contains values > 0.20 within the last 5 days.",
    "Horizon-Specific Overshoot: The model's linear extrapolation causes it to miss the peak and subsequent crash in the mid-forecast horizon (days 10-20). Correction: Implement a non-linear decay function that reduces the forecast slope as the predicted price approaches historical resistance levels (e.g., >95 EUR).",
    "Failure to Capture Downward Drift: After the 100 EUR peak, the model continues to project stability or slight growth, missing the sustained downward drift to ~88 EUR. Correction: Apply a mean-reversion pull towards the 20-day moving average once the forecast exceeds the current spot price by >3%."
  ]
}
